            <ArticleTitle>Hemicrania continua: a case in which a patient experienced complete relief on melatonin.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>524-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper reports a case of hemicrania continua in which attacks were successfully eliminated while taking melatonin 7 mg at bedtime after the patient was no longer able to tolerate indomethacin due to gastrointestinal side effects.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
